# Read-aloud voices, with the test engine only (run.sh uses it; the system's voices differ
# from one system to another): the most natural voice for the text's language reads
# without being chosen (the test engine has a robotic voice and natural English and French
# ones); the bar's voice menu lists them, and the voice chosen there reads and is kept.
cursor off
open "$SAMPLES/tagged.pdf"
wait 800
assert speech.available == true
key ctrl+shift+v
await speech.playing == false 60000
assert speech.voice == Natural English
assert speech.voice-name == Natural English
click "Voice" 300
await speech.voices contains Robot 5000
wait 200
screenshot 37-voices.png
# The menu opens on the voice chosen, Automatic; Robot is two rows down.
key down
key down
key return
wait 200
assert speech.voice-name == Robot
call speech-clear
page 1
wait 400
key ctrl+shift+v
await speech.playing == false 60000
assert speech.voice == Robot
click "Voice" 300
wait 200
key up
key up
key return
wait 200
assert speech.voice-name == Natural English
